[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: NexRT Implementation Requirements
UID: NXR-BASELINE
VERSION: 2026-10-18

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-001
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Boot registry seal
STATEMENT: >>>
The kernel shall register application threads only before start, within a configured finite capacity, using permanent caller-provided control blocks and stacks.
Acceptance: Exactly RTOS_MAX_THREADS unique registrations succeed; duplicate, excess and post-start calls fail unchanged; zero application threads starts idle.
Verification: Host capacity/duplicate tests and target registration API/seal tests.
Configuration: RTOS_MAX_THREADS 1..255.
Static budget: Configured application pointer table plus one private idle thread.
Dependencies: 
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-002
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Static resource lifetimes
STATEMENT: >>>
The kernel shall retain boot resource ownership metadata through shutdown and neither allocate nor free general heap storage during initialization or execution.
Acceptance: Firmware passes no-heap audit; repeated completion, IPC, timer and network operations preserve capacities and storage addresses; finished storage stays reserved.
Verification: ELF audit, ownership review and target resource-inventory stress.
Configuration: All enabled features.
Static budget: Zero general heap bytes; boot-fixed capacities.
Dependencies: NXR-001
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-003
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Stack registration bounds
STATEMENT: >>>
Registration shall reject invalid stack alignment, insufficient size, address overflow and stack/control-block overlap before changing state.
Acceptance: Reject size below 512, size/alignment not divisible by 16, overflowing ranges and overlap; accept touching ranges; failures preserve registry/control contents.
Verification: Host boundary tests and target registration failure atomicity.
Configuration: Minimum 512 bytes; alignment 16.
Static budget: One scan of configured registered ranges.
Dependencies: NXR-001
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-004
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Strict priority dispatch
STATEMENT: >>>
At each dispatch the scheduler shall select the ready application thread with greatest effective priority and use idle only when no application is ready.
Acceptance: Finite reference-model comparison never selects a lower ready priority; priority-zero work precedes idle; higher-priority wakeup wins next dispatch.
Verification: Host small-state model and target wakeup/idle tests.
Configuration: Priorities 0..255; larger first.
Static budget: At most RTOS_MAX_THREADS candidates per selection.
Dependencies: NXR-001
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-005
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Equal-priority fairness
STATEMENT: >>>
Timer round robin shall rotate equal-priority ready peers when enabled; explicit yield shall rotate peers in either configuration.
Acceptance: N ready peers each run once in N rotations; slicing disabled retains current peer unless higher priority ready; yield rotates in both modes.
Verification: Peer counts, cursor wrap, blocked peers and target timer slicing tests.
Configuration: RTOS_ROUND_ROBIN = 0 or 1.
Static budget: Existing registry and one cursor; no extra allocations.
Dependencies: NXR-004
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-006
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Priority changes
STATEMENT: >>>
The priority API shall atomically update a registered live thread base priority and reconsider scheduling before returning when running while preserving active inheritance.
Acceptance: Unregistered/finished fail unchanged; boot/sleeping changes succeed; lowering current permits higher-priority peer before return; preserve donations.
Verification: Target priority changes, invalid IDs, sleeping and donated-priority cases.
Configuration: Base/effective priorities 0..255.
Static budget: Recomputation bounded by thread/mutex capacities.
Dependencies: NXR-004
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-007
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Integer context preservation
STATEMENT: >>>
The RISCue trap boundary shall preserve interrupted integer registers, continuation PC, stack pointer and machine status across preemption and yields with 16-byte C++ call alignment.
Acceptance: Distinct register patterns survive 100000 timer preemptions and yields with zero PC, stack, register or interrupt-state mismatches.
Verification: Assembly-assisted target register stress with nested C++ calls and canaries.
Configuration: Single-hart RV32 integer machine mode; no FP/vector.
Static budget: 144-byte frame plus analyzed kernel call depth.
Dependencies: NXR-004
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-008
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Inline assembly compiler contracts
STATEMENT: >>>
CSR and critical-section inline assembly shall declare correct operands and ordering; standalone assembly shall be limited to startup and asynchronous entry/restore.
Acceptance: Every supported optimized configuration preserves context/API results; disassembly retains approved CSR operands and ordering.
Verification: Compiler/disassembly review and target optimization/LTO matrix when supported.
Configuration: Documented optimization/compiler configurations.
Static budget: No new runtime storage; fixed assembly boundaries.
Dependencies: NXR-007
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-009
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Relative sleep wrap semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
Relative sleep shall accept 0..INT32_MAX ticks, treat zero as yield, reject larger delays and use wrap-safe deadlines.
Acceptance: Cover 0, 1, INT32_MAX, INT32_MAX+1 and wrap across UINT32_MAX; rejected calls do not block or mutate state.
Verification: Host modular arithmetic and target sleep API boundary tests.
Configuration: 32-bit ticks; relative delay at most INT32_MAX.
Static budget: One deadline/thread; one bounded wake scan.
Dependencies: NXR-004
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-010
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Delayed timer catch-up
STATEMENT: >>>
Timer handling shall compute missed periods arithmetically, scan sleepers once per delivered interrupt and reject catch-up beyond the modular horizon.
Acceptance: 1, 10, 1000000 missed periods require one scan with model-equivalent wakes; greater than INT32_MAX invokes fault policy.
Verification: Scan-count instrumentation and masked-interrupt/exact-boundary/horizon target tests.
Configuration: Nonzero integer timer period; half-range horizon.
Static budget: One arithmetic catch-up and one thread scan.
Dependencies: NXR-009
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-011
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Timer MMIO integrity
STATEMENT: >>>
The timer port shall read a coherent 64-bit monotonic clock and update compare without exposing a transient earlier deadline.
Acceptance: Rollover reads are coherent; compare writes high-max, low, final-high; diagnostics report actual integer period.
Verification: Instrumented MMIO and target rollover/write-order tests.
Configuration: Timer/compare addresses and supplied clock/tick rates.
Static budget: Three compare writes; read retry assumptions documented for hardware.
Dependencies: NXR-010
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-012
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Absolute periodic release
STATEMENT: >>>
The kernel shall provide absolute sleep and a static periodic helper advancing from prior intended deadlines with missed-release reporting.
Acceptance: Variable work preserves original release grid; overdue activity skips to next future release and counts misses; reject zero/half-range-invalid periods; support wrap.
Verification: On-time, missed-release, wrap and invalid-period tests.
Configuration: Optional helper; period 1..INT32_MAX; saturating miss counter.
Static budget: Fixed state per boot-created periodic activity.
Dependencies: NXR-009
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-013
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Interrupt-state restoration
STATEMENT: >>>
Kernel-private critical sections shall preserve prior interrupt state across internal scheduler transitions; while scheduling is active, public blocking or scheduling calls shall reject application-disabled interrupt context before changing thread state.
Acceptance: Nested private locks restore prior MIE without enabling early. Internal sleep/resume preserves its private lock state. Application-held interrupt masking followed by sleep, yield, exit or a rescheduling priority change is rejected through a documented error or fault without a partial state transition; pre-start boot configuration remains legal.
Verification: Target nested-lock/blocking/preemption MIE observation.
Configuration: Single hart; no implicit interrupt nesting.
Static budget: One saved status word per lock; nesting bounded by reviewed call depth.
Dependencies: NXR-007
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-014
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Interrupt dispatcher boundary
STATEMENT: >>>
The port shall dispatch registered supported sources, acknowledge through a board contract and route unsupported sources/exceptions to bounded fault handling.
Acceptance: One handler/source; invalid/spurious IDs cannot call arbitrary memory or loop indefinitely; acknowledgment permits subsequent interrupts.
Verification: External, invalid, spurious, disabled and repeated acknowledgment tests.
Configuration: Fixed boot source capacity and board acknowledgment operations.
Static budget: Fixed source table and bounded handling/acknowledgment.
Dependencies: NXR-007
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-015
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Deferred interrupt work
STATEMENT: >>>
Drivers shall signal boot-created deferred workers through explicit ISR APIs with fixed storage and bounded nonblocking operations.
Acceptance: No ISR allocation/wait; full capacity returns result and increments overflow; accepted work wakes worker without lost signals.
Verification: Burst, full, coalescing, wakeup and forbidden blocking-context tests.
Configuration: Optional worker count, queue capacity and coalescing policy.
Static budget: Boot worker stacks and fixed pending-work slots.
Dependencies: NXR-014, NXR-020
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-016
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Static mutex ownership
STATEMENT: >>>
Boot-initialized mutexes shall enforce a single owner, reject non-owner unlock and provide nonrecursive try, timed and blocking acquisition.
Acceptance: One owner maximum; recursive acquisition reports error; timeout/unlock races preserve ownership; invalid/ISR/pre-start calls leave state consistent.
Verification: Contention, recursion, wrong-owner, timeout-race and context-misuse tests.
Configuration: Optional fixed mutex capacity; nonrecursive initially.
Static budget: One owner/control record per mutex; bounded thread waiters.
Dependencies: NXR-001, NXR-009, NXR-020
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-017
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Transitive priority inheritance
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutex contention shall raise effective priorities to active donation maxima, propagate through bounded chains and recompute when donations end.
Acceptance: H/L contention preempts M; H/L/X propagation works; timeout, unlock and base-priority changes recompute every held mutex without stale donations.
Verification: H/M/L, chained, multiple-owner, withdrawal and base-priority change tests.
Configuration: Mutex inheritance with priorities 0..255.
Static budget: Traversal bounded by thread/mutex capacities; static graph storage.
Dependencies: NXR-004, NXR-016
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-018
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Mutex deadlock and owner termination
STATEMENT: >>>
Mutex acquisition shall detect wait-for cycles before blocking, and owner exit shall fault deterministically without silently releasing ownership.
Acceptance: Two/three-thread cycles return deadlock; maximum-depth search terminates; owner return/exit records fault without ownership transfer.
Verification: Cycle, maximum-chain and owner-return/exit fault tests.
Configuration: Documented deadlock error and owner-exit fault policy.
Static budget: At most RTOS_MAX_THREADS search nodes; fixed fault storage.
Dependencies: NXR-016, NXR-017
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-019
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Counting and binary semaphores
STATEMENT: >>>
Static semaphores shall enforce maximum count and offer try, timed, blocking take and bounded thread/ISR release with overflow results.
Acceptance: Count within 0..max; overflow fails; timeout/release resolves exactly once; priority waiters and ISR rescheduling follow policy.
Verification: Zero/max/overflow, waiter ordering, timeout-race and ISR tests.
Configuration: Optional boot counts/max; binary maximum 1.
Static budget: Fixed records and one wait membership/thread.
Dependencies: NXR-009, NXR-014, NXR-020
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-020
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Atomic bounded wait lifecycle
STATEMENT: >>>
Blocking primitives shall atomically register waiters, transition state and resolve wakeup, timeout or cancellation exactly once in fixed waiter storage.
Acceptance: Signal-before/after-enqueue and timeout ties resolve once; no duplicate memberships; capacity never exceeds thread count.
Verification: Deterministic scheduling/reference interleavings and repeated reuse.
Configuration: Shared substrate for all blocking features.
Static budget: One active wait record/thread; bounded object wait queues.
Dependencies: NXR-001, NXR-004, NXR-009
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-021
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Event flags semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
Enabled event groups shall support a configured width of 1..32 bits, a boot-declared reserved-bit mask, any/all waits, and optional clear-on-exit evaluated in descending effective priority with FIFO ordering among equal-priority waiters.
Acceptance: Reject masks outside the configured width or containing reserved bits. Process waiters in priority/FIFO order against the remaining flags. For a satisfied clear-on-exit waiter, consume requested bits currently set (any) or all requested bits (all) before evaluating the next waiter; nonclearing waiters leave flags unchanged. Exhaustive 3-bit models cover consumption, simultaneous waiters and timeout/ISR-set races.
Verification: Small-width exhaustive combinations, multiwaiter, timeout and ISR-set tests.
Configuration: RTOS_EVENT_BITS = 1..32; boot reserved mask; priority/FIFO waiter order; explicit clear-on-exit.
Static budget: Fixed flag/control record per group; bounded thread waiters.
Dependencies: NXR-014, NXR-020
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-022
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Typed fixed-capacity queues
STATEMENT: >>>
Queues shall hold a compile-time bounded number of trivially copyable messages in caller storage with FIFO send/receive and full, empty, timeout results.
Acceptance: Capacity N accepts exactly N pending messages; FIFO survives wrap/multiple producers/consumers; rejected sends preserve data; invalid types/sizes/alignment fail compilation.
Verification: Capacity 1/N, wrap, full/empty, concurrency, payload and compile-fail tests.
Configuration: Optional payload type and positive static capacity.
Static budget: N times payload bytes plus fixed metadata and bounded waiters.
Dependencies: NXR-001, NXR-020
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-023
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: ISR-safe queue subset
STATEMENT: >>>
ISR queues shall use explicit nonblocking APIs, bounded copies, immediate capacity errors and interrupt-return higher-priority rescheduling.
Acceptance: Maximum copy bounded; failed full/empty leaves state intact; accepted messages survive IRQ/consumer races; highest-ready worker runs next legal return.
Verification: Maximum-payload, full/empty, interleaving, scheduling and misuse tests.
Configuration: Explicit ISR subset and maximum payload bytes.
Static budget: One configured bounded payload copy and fixed metadata changes.
Dependencies: NXR-014, NXR-022
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-024
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Static software timers
STATEMENT: >>>
Software timers shall use boot-reserved records, one-shot/periodic modes, bounded expiration processing and boot-created callback workers outside ISR.
Acceptance: Capacity exhaustion returns an error. Periodic timers retain the intended release grid and allow at most one pending invocation per timer; excess expirations coalesce and increment a saturating 32-bit unsigned missed-expiration counter. Cancellation of a queued but not executing callback prevents its start and returns Cancelled. Cancellation during execution returns Busy without changing its schedule; caller may retry. Cancel/restart/expire races produce exactly one documented result; callbacks run only in worker context.
Verification: Capacity, cancel/expire, restart, wrap, long-callback, backlog and context tests.
Configuration: Optional timer count and worker priority/stack; one pending callback per timer; 32-bit unsigned saturating miss counter; explicit Cancelled/Busy results.
Static budget: Fixed records/callback queue; scan bounded by configured timer count.
Dependencies: NXR-012, NXR-015, NXR-020
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-025
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Bounded work and timing evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Every kernel API and IRQ path shall document work bounds, forbid unbounded callbacks under interrupt masking and expose measured dispatch/interrupt-disabled latency per supported release profile.
Acceptance: Every operation has a finite count-based bound; max-capacity reports pin compiler, configuration, workload and observed durations; explicit application thresholds gate release without a formal WCET claim.
Verification: Instrument worst capacities, wait chains, snapshot sizes and timer backlog on target; archive logs.
Configuration: All supported profiles; application-defined latency thresholds.
Static budget: Bounds use fixed thread, mutex, timer, queue and snapshot capacities; fixed instrumentation storage.
Dependencies: NXR-004, NXR-010, NXR-013, NXR-017, NXR-020, NXR-024
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-026
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Boot device registry
STATEMENT: >>>
The device registry shall accept unique boot-defined names and static driver objects before sealing at scheduler start.
Acceptance: Duplicate names, null operation tables, capacity overflow and post-start registration fail unchanged; lookup returns the exact registered instance or not-found.
Verification: Registry capacity, duplicate, seal and lookup tests.
Configuration: Optional devices; positive maximum device count; names at most 31 bytes.
Static budget: Fixed registry entries and copied bounded names; zero runtime allocation.
Dependencies: NXR-001
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-027
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Unified device operations
STATEMENT: >>>
Devices shall expose bounded read, write and typed control operations returning status and transferred byte count, with explicit nonblocking or absolute-deadline modes.
Acceptance: Unsupported operations return not-supported; zero-length operations transfer zero; short transfers report exact progress; expired deadlines never wait; control rejects unknown commands and incorrect payload sizes unchanged.
Verification: Mock-driver short transfer, unsupported, deadline and control validation tests.
Configuration: Fixed operation table per device; finite control command set.
Static budget: Caller buffers accessed only during synchronous ownership; abort-uncertain DMA uses fixed driver-owned staging; request state and concurrent operations boot-bounded.
Dependencies: NXR-009, NXR-013, NXR-020, NXR-026
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-028
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded descriptor handles
STATEMENT: >>>
Opening a device or file shall acquire a slot from a boot-reserved descriptor table and return an index-plus-generation handle.
Acceptance: Exactly configured slot count opens succeed; excess returns resource-exhausted; close/reopen invalidates old handles; generations never wrap into reuse because exhausted-generation slots retire until reboot.
Verification: Exhaustion, stale handle, invalid index and near-generation-limit tests.
Configuration: Optional descriptors; configured slot count; 32-bit generation.
Static budget: Fixed descriptor records; no heap; retired slots remain counted unavailable.
Dependencies: NXR-026, NXR-027
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-029
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Descriptor close lifecycle
STATEMENT: >>>
Close shall mark a valid descriptor closing, reject new operations, wait only until its supplied deadline for in-flight operations and release the slot exactly once after quiescence.
Acceptance: Close after successful completion returns invalid-handle. Concurrent close while another close call is active returns Busy. A timed-out close retains Closing state and permits a later same-handle close retry after the first call returns. New I/O is rejected in Closing. Quiescent cleanup releases the slot exactly once; driver-close failure quarantines a diagnosable unavailable slot.
Verification: Close versus read/write races, timeout retry and injected close-failure tests.
Configuration: Finite per-slot active-operation counter; close uses absolute deadline.
Static budget: Fixed closing state and active count per descriptor; no detached cleanup allocation.
Dependencies: NXR-028, NXR-020
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-030
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded pathname resolution
STATEMENT: >>>
The VFS shall accept explicit bounded byte-span paths, normalize absolute paths with repeated separators and dot components, and reject embedded NUL bytes, traversal above root and symbolic links.
Acceptance: Validate the complete supplied byte span, including bytes after any embedded NUL. Reject excessive span/component lengths before provider calls. /a/../b resolves to /b; /../b and relative paths fail invalid-path; no symbolic links are followed.
Verification: Path normalization model and malformed/boundary input tests.
Configuration: Optional VFS; positive maximum path bytes, component bytes and component count.
Static budget: Fixed normalization workspace per configured concurrent resolver; traversal bounded by component count.
Dependencies: NXR-026
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-031
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Static device filesystem
STATEMENT: >>>
A devfs provider shall expose sealed device-registry entries under /dev and route opens through descriptor ownership rules.
Acceptance: Every registered exported device appears once; unknown names return not-found; directory iteration is bounded and stable; create, unlink and rename return read-only.
Verification: Registry-to-devfs mapping, stable enumeration and forbidden mutation tests.
Configuration: Optional devfs; boot export flag per device.
Static budget: No duplicated driver objects; at most one fixed directory record per exported device.
Dependencies: NXR-026, NXR-028, NXR-030
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-032
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Read-only ROM filesystem
STATEMENT: >>>
A ROM filesystem shall expose a boot-linked immutable file table with bounded offset reads and no executable loading.
Acceptance: Reads at EOF return zero; short tail reads are exact; overflowing offsets and invalid table ranges fail; all writes and namespace mutations return read-only; content bytes match linked assets.
Verification: ROM image table validation, offset boundaries and content checksum tests.
Configuration: Optional ROMFS; fixed file count and linked asset byte budget.
Static budget: Immutable table and linked bytes; per-open offset stored in descriptor slot.
Dependencies: NXR-028, NXR-030
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-033
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded RAM filesystem
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional RAMFS shall use boot-reserved inode and data-block pools, permit only regular files and directories and return explicit exhaustion without growing storage.
Acceptance: Inode/block exhaustion leaves existing contents intact; writes may return documented exact short counts; unlink of open files reclaims blocks only after last close; truncate zeroes newly visible bytes; reboot discards contents.
Verification: Pool exhaustion, short write, open-unlink, truncate and repeated create/delete conservation tests.
Configuration: Optional RAMFS; fixed inode count, block size, block count and directory-entry capacity.
Static budget: Exactly configured inode, directory and block pools; ownership counters conserve every slot.
Dependencies: NXR-028, NXR-029, NXR-030
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-034
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Boot mount table
STATEMENT: >>>
Mounts shall be registered only at boot with unique absolute normalized prefixes, then remain immutable; resolution shall select the longest component-boundary prefix.
Acceptance: Duplicate prefixes and mount-table overflow fail; /rom does not match /romance; nested mount chooses longest match; runtime mount/unmount returns sealed.
Verification: Prefix boundary, nested mount, duplicate, capacity and boot seal tests.
Configuration: Fixed mount count; optional devfs, ROMFS and RAMFS providers.
Static budget: Fixed mount table and bounded copied prefixes; lookup scans at most configured mounts.
Dependencies: NXR-030, NXR-031, NXR-032
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-035
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Static byte pipes
STATEMENT: >>>
A pipe shall use a boot-reserved byte ring and bounded endpoint slots, provide partial FIFO transfers and resolve endpoint closure without dynamic allocation.
Acceptance: Empty pipe with writers returns would-block or waits to deadline; empty pipe without writers returns EOF; write without readers returns broken-pipe; close wakes affected waiters; byte order survives ring wrap.
Verification: Ring wrap, full/empty, deadline, endpoint-close races and endpoint exhaustion tests.
Configuration: Optional pipes; fixed pipe count, bytes per pipe and reader/writer endpoint limits.
Static budget: Fixed rings and endpoint records; total queued bytes never exceeds configured storage.
Dependencies: NXR-020, NXR-028, NXR-029
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-036
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Built-in command registry
STATEMENT: >>>
The shell shall dispatch only a sealed boot-defined table of built-in C++ command functions with unique bounded names.
Acceptance: Duplicate/overlong names fail at boot; unknown commands return command-not-found; dispatch invokes only registered pointers; registry overflow fails unchanged.
Verification: Registry validation, unknown command and dispatch identity tests.
Configuration: Optional shell; fixed command count and maximum command-name bytes.
Static budget: Fixed command table; all command code linked into firmware.
Dependencies: NXR-026
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-037
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded shell parser
STATEMENT: >>>
The shell shall parse bounded lines with whitespace separation, single/double quoted arguments and backslash escapes, rejecting unsupported expansion, redirection and pipeline syntax initially.
Acceptance: Reject oversized lines, excessive arguments, unmatched quotes and trailing escapes before execution. Preserve quoted spaces and empty arguments. Unquoted expansion, redirection and pipeline metacharacters return parse errors; quoted or escaped metacharacters are literal bytes and never trigger expansion or execution.
Verification: Grammar corpus, boundary tests and deterministic fuzzing against reference parser.
Configuration: Fixed maximum line bytes and argument count; no environment expansion or command substitution.
Static budget: One fixed line buffer and argument-index array per shell session.
Dependencies: NXR-036
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-038
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Static shell sessions
STATEMENT: >>>
Each enabled shell session shall own boot-reserved input/output buffers and a boot-created worker, with bounded editing and output backpressure.
Acceptance: Session capacity is fixed; line overflow discards until newline and reports one error; output waits only to deadline and reports truncation; disconnected sessions release no borrowed buffer prematurely.
Verification: Maximum sessions, oversized line recovery, slow output and disconnect tests.
Configuration: Fixed session count, worker priority/stack and input/output ring bytes.
Static budget: Exactly configured session buffers and stacks; no runtime worker creation.
Dependencies: NXR-027, NXR-036, NXR-037
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-039
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Jobs on boot workers
STATEMENT: >>>
Background commands shall run only on a fixed boot-created worker pool with generation-tagged job slots and cooperative cancellation.
Acceptance: Pool exhaustion returns Busy. Jobs run on permanent workers that return to their dispatch loop, never exit. Generation-tagged stale IDs fail; generation-exhausted slots retire until reboot. Cancellation is cooperative without forced unwinding; uncooperative jobs remain occupied and become Stuck after the configured grace interval.
Verification: Pool exhaustion, stale IDs, completion/cancel races and noncooperating-job tests.
Configuration: Optional jobs; fixed worker/job count, stacks and cancellation grace ticks.
Static budget: One permanent stack/control block per worker plus fixed job records and bounded copied arguments.
Dependencies: NXR-001, NXR-020, NXR-036, NXR-038
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-040
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded diagnostic commands
STATEMENT: >>>
Built-in ps, top, uptime and devices commands shall consume coherent bounded snapshots and print explicit truncation indicators without holding kernel locks during formatting or output.
Acceptance: ps reports name/state/base/effective priority; top handles zero elapsed time and disabled metrics explicitly; rows never exceed caller capacity; slow console output occurs after snapshot lock release.
Verification: Snapshot-to-command golden outputs, truncation, disabled metrics and slow-console instrumentation.
Configuration: Optional diagnostics; fixed maximum rows and output bytes per command invocation.
Static budget: Fixed snapshot rows and formatting buffer per session; one snapshot per refresh.
Dependencies: NXR-006, NXR-026, NXR-036, NXR-038
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-041
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: UART bounded transport
STATEMENT: >>>
The UART driver shall use fixed RX/TX rings, expose nonblocking/deadline transfers and defer interrupt processing through approved bounded paths.
Acceptance: RX overflow drops newest byte and increments a saturating counter; TX full returns short count or waits only to deadline; framing/parity/overrun errors are counted; loopback preserves accepted byte order.
Verification: Hardware/model loopback, ring saturation, error injection and deadline tests.
Configuration: Optional UART instances; fixed ring bytes, baud and framing selected at boot.
Static budget: Fixed per-instance rings/control state; ISR work capped at configured bytes per interrupt.
Dependencies: NXR-014, NXR-015, NXR-027
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-042
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Console routing and fault output
STATEMENT: >>>
Console input/output shall route to one boot-selected device; panic output shall use a bounded polling path with a fixed byte/time limit and no descriptor locks.
Acceptance: Normal output follows device backpressure; panic writes at most configured bytes and stops at deadline or unavailable device; recursive panic terminates immediately without lock acquisition.
Verification: Slow/stuck UART, recursive panic and scheduler-disabled output tests.
Configuration: One boot console; optional panic output with positive byte and tick/cycle limits.
Static budget: Fixed panic buffer and recursion flag; no worker or memory acquisition in panic.
Dependencies: NXR-027, NXR-041
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-043
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: GPIO ownership and safe state
STATEMENT: >>>
GPIO shall enforce boot-declared pin ownership, validated direction/functions and board-defined safe output values on failed initialization or explicit shutdown.
Acceptance: Conflicting claims and unsupported pin/function fail before hardware changes; writes affect only owned pins; output values are established before enabling drive; failure restores declared safe state.
Verification: Mock-register ownership/mask tests and board safe-state measurements.
Configuration: Optional fixed pin table and owner map; board safe values required for outputs.
Static budget: One fixed record per declared pin; no runtime pin claims.
Dependencies: NXR-026, NXR-027
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-044
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: SPI bounded transactions
STATEMENT: >>>
SPI shall accept transactions from fixed boot request slots, serialize each bus and hold chip select only for one bounded transaction with an absolute completion deadline.
Acceptance: Validate mode/rate/length before assertion; preserve segment order; queue full returns busy; timeout deasserts chip select and returns transferred count; subsequent requests recover or receive unavailable.
Verification: Mode validation, contention, full queue, timeout and chip-select waveform tests.
Configuration: Optional buses; fixed request count, maximum segments/bytes and supported rates/modes.
Static budget: Fixed request/control slots and boot driver-owned DMA staging; hardware cannot retain caller or stack buffer references after any return, including errors.
Dependencies: NXR-009, NXR-016, NXR-026, NXR-027
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-045
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: I2C error and recovery bounds
STATEMENT: >>>
I2C shall serialize bounded address transactions, report NACK/arbitration/timeout distinctly and attempt at most nine recovery clocks followed by STOP before marking a stuck bus unavailable.
Acceptance: Invalid addresses/lengths fail before START; repeated-start sequences preserve atomic ownership; NACK returns exact progress; recovery is attempted once per failed transaction and never exceeds deadline; unavailable buses reject requests until explicit bounded reinitialize.
Verification: NACK, arbitration loss, clock stretch, stuck SDA and recovery waveform tests.
Configuration: Optional buses; fixed request count/bytes; standard 7-bit addressing initially.
Static budget: Fixed transaction slots and one bus recovery state per instance.
Dependencies: NXR-009, NXR-016, NXR-026, NXR-027
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-046
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Progress-based watchdog supervision
STATEMENT: >>>
A boot-created supervisor shall feed the hardware watchdog only when every enabled critical thread advances its registered progress token within its configured monotonic interval.
Acceptance: A stuck critical worker prevents feeding by its deadline; token wrap is handled; noncritical workers do not inhibit feeding; first missed participant is recorded before reset; watchdog setup is validated against supervisor period.
Verification: Stalled worker, interrupt-only activity, token wrap, false-positive margin and actual reset tests.
Configuration: Optional supervisor; fixed critical participant list and positive per-participant deadlines.
Static budget: Fixed token/deadline records plus one boot supervisor stack; one scan per supervision period.
Dependencies: NXR-001, NXR-009, NXR-012, NXR-026
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-047
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Ordered driver boot failure
STATEMENT: >>>
Drivers shall initialize through a fixed dependency-ordered boot table; critical failure shall abort startup and reverse-unwind every initialized driver, while optional failure shall clean up that partially initialized driver, skip transitive dependents and retain successful providers.
Acceptance: Reject cycles and unknown dependencies before hardware access. Run partial-driver cleanup even when initialization fails. Critical failure prevents start and cleans initialized drivers once in reverse order. Optional failure cleans only the failed partial driver, skips dependents and retains initialized shared providers. Every cleanup has a deadline; cleanup failure records a fault and preserves safe/unavailable state.
Verification: Dependency graph validation and failure injection at every boot-table position.
Configuration: Fixed init entry count; critical/optional classification and bounded init/shutdown deadlines.
Static budget: Fixed table and visited/state arrays; traversal bounded by configured entries/edges.
Dependencies: NXR-026, NXR-043
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-048
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Device request cancellation
STATEMENT: >>>
Timed device operations shall return only after hardware has no reference to caller buffers; abort-uncertain DMA hardware shall use boot driver-owned staging or fail driver initialization, and failed abort shall quarantine its request/staging slot.
Acceptance: Both success and fault returns leave caller storage safe to reuse. Abort-uncertain hardware never receives caller addresses. Failed abort retains only driver-owned staging and quarantines it with a distinct fault result. Late completions cannot target reused generations; repeated abort is idempotent.
Verification: Delayed DMA completion, abort success/failure, stale completion and slot quarantine tests.
Configuration: Fixed abort deadline and request-generation width; asynchronous drivers use driver-owned buffers.
Static budget: Fixed request slots and staging buffers; quarantined capacity never silently reused.
Dependencies: NXR-027, NXR-029
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-049
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded readiness polling
STATEMENT: >>>
A readiness API shall inspect a bounded caller-supplied descriptor set for read/write/error readiness and wait atomically to a deadline without consuming data.
Acceptance: Oversized sets fail before driver calls; already-ready returns immediately; readiness transition between registration and sleep is not lost; closed/stale handles report per-entry error; timeout returns zero ready entries.
Verification: Ready-before-wait, transition race, close race, invalid handle and maximum-set tests.
Configuration: Optional readiness; configured maximum descriptors per wait.
Static budget: One boot-reserved readiness record per waiting thread and bounded descriptor indices.
Dependencies: NXR-020, NXR-027, NXR-028, NXR-029
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-050
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Coherent device diagnostics
STATEMENT: >>>
Each driver shall expose a bounded typed health snapshot containing availability, fault reason, capacity/occupancy, overflow/error counts and reset generation without clearing counters on read.
Acceptance: Snapshots are internally coherent; counters saturate at maximum rather than wrap; repeated reads have no reset side effect; disabled features return not-supported; fixed output truncation reports required/written rows.
Verification: Concurrent update/snapshot, saturation, disabled driver and bounded enumeration tests.
Configuration: Optional device metrics with fixed per-driver schema and maximum snapshot rows.
Static budget: Fixed per-device counters/state and caller-owned snapshot rows; no formatting under driver locks.
Dependencies: NXR-026, NXR-027, NXR-047
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-051
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Ethernet adapter boot contract
STATEMENT: >>>
The Ethernet adapter shall initialize once at boot with complete MAC/input callbacks and preserve state on invalid or repeated initialization.
Acceptance: Missing callbacks and second initialization fail unchanged; before initialization link is false, poll returns zero and send errors; callback context remains valid for adapter lifetime.
Verification: Initialization boundaries and target callback-lifetime review.
Configuration: Optional RTOS_ETHERNET; fixed adapter instance count.
Static budget: One permanent 1536-byte RX scratch buffer and fixed callback/statistics state per instance.
Dependencies: NXR-001, NXR-002
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-052
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Bounded Ethernet RX validation
STATEMENT: >>>
RX polling shall attempt at most its supplied budget, stop on empty/busy/error and reject frames outside 14..1536 bytes before protocol delivery.
Acceptance: Budget zero invokes no receive; N budget invokes at most N receives; malformed lengths never reach input; hardware callbacks never write beyond supplied capacity; errors terminate the call.
Verification: Budget/length boundaries, malformed frames and guarded-buffer MAC tests.
Configuration: Per-call receive budget; standard/tagged frames without FCS; no jumbo support.
Static budget: One fixed scratch frame; no per-frame allocation; callback execution independently bounded.
Dependencies: NXR-051
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-053
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Ethernet TX staging and backpressure
STATEMENT: >>>
Transmit shall consume/copy valid caller bytes before return, return busy without retaining caller pointers and use boot-reserved staging for asynchronous hardware.
Acceptance: Null/invalid lengths error; accepted send permits immediate caller reuse; busy consumes no caller ownership; full staging returns busy; completion returns each slot exactly once.
Verification: Caller overwrite, staging exhaustion, duplicate/late completion and retry tests.
Configuration: Configured TX staging slots and maximum 1536-byte frame.
Static budget: Fixed staging frames and completion metadata; no pool growth.
Dependencies: NXR-048, NXR-051
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-054
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: DMA ring ownership and coherency
STATEMENT: >>>
MAC DMA shall use aligned boot-reserved rings with free, hardware-owned, completed and quarantined states and board-provided cache/barrier operations.
Acceptance: Every descriptor has one owner; handoff barriers precede ownership bits; cache operations respect lines; duplicate completion faults; abort failure quarantines until reset quiescence.
Verification: DMA ownership model, barrier instrumentation and saturation/reset tests.
Configuration: Board alignment/cache requirements and fixed RX/TX descriptor counts.
Static budget: Fixed aligned rings and packet storage; ownership-state counts equal configured slots.
Dependencies: NXR-048, NXR-053
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-055
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: PHY and MDIO deadlines
STATEMENT: >>>
PHY management shall perform finite MDIO transactions and deadline-bounded reset/autonegotiation, returning unavailable on unsupported identity or deadline expiration.
Acceptance: Stuck-busy transactions expire; invalid address fails before access; reset/negotiation respect absolute deadlines; unsupported PHY never enables traffic.
Verification: Busy, missing-PHY, identity and negotiation timeout tests.
Configuration: Optional PHY; fixed address and supported identity table.
Static budget: Fixed transaction state and one sampled link record per interface.
Dependencies: NXR-009, NXR-026, NXR-027
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-056
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Link transition state machine
STATEMENT: >>>
The network owner shall process down, negotiating, up and fault transitions, reject new TX while down and quiesce ownership before recycling buffers.
Acceptance: Down rejects send; pending TX completes/errors once; repeated flaps conserve slots; stale generations fail; link reads never wait for negotiation.
Verification: Cable flap, pending-TX loss, stale completion and recovery tests.
Configuration: Fixed interfaces and bounded transition/recovery deadlines.
Static budget: One fixed state/generation record per interface; no reconnect allocation.
Dependencies: NXR-054, NXR-055
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-057
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Single network-owner worker
STATEMENT: >>>
Each stack instance shall confine MAC polling, protocol entry, timers and stack statistics to one boot-created worker; other threads shall submit bounded requests.
Acceptance: Wrong-worker/recursive entry is rejected or trapped in development; ISR only signals work; full requests return busy. Pending RX, requests and timers each receive a nonzero bounded service budget. At the configured maximum worker residency, remaining work is retained and the worker blocks for at least one tick to permit lower-priority progress. Profiles whose protocol deadlines cannot tolerate this reservation are rejected.
Verification: Owner/reentrancy misuse, concurrent requests and bounded fairness tests.
Configuration: Fixed worker priority/stack, nonzero RX/request/timer budgets and maximum residency plus mandatory blocking interval.
Static budget: One boot stack plus fixed request/completion queues per stack.
Dependencies: NXR-015, NXR-022, NXR-051
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-058
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Existing stack integration seam
STATEMENT: >>>
An optional existing TCP/IP stack shall integrate behind a version-pinned C/C++ adapter with boot-reserved pools and audited ownership paths.
Acceptance: Chosen version/config cross-builds; forbidden allocator symbols absent; each retained packet has bounded owner/release paths; disabling stack removes code/pools.
Verification: Pinned-stack build, negative allocation fixture and ownership audit.
Configuration: Optional raw single-owner stack initially; no blanket POSIX claim.
Static budget: Explicit pool/table budgets; link fits selected board RAM; no claim full networking fits default RAM.
Dependencies: NXR-002, NXR-057
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-059
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Protocol timer servicing
STATEMENT: >>>
The network worker shall service protocol deadlines from monotonic kernel time with a finite due-work budget each iteration and no timer reset.
Acceptance: Wrap-safe due times; floods cannot postpone timers beyond configured service budget; excess work is counted and continued next loop; callbacks only in owner context.
Verification: Flood, timer burst, wrap and owner-context tests.
Configuration: Fixed maximum timers and per-loop timer budget.
Static budget: Boot timer records; at most configured callbacks per loop.
Dependencies: NXR-009, NXR-012, NXR-057, NXR-058
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-060
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Packet pool conservation
STATEMENT: >>>
Packet storage shall use boot-reserved pools with bounded runtime loans, validated ownership transitions and explicit exhaustion results.
Acceptance: Free+loaned+hardware+quarantined counts equal capacity; double release/foreign pointers fail; exhaustion drops/rejects with counters; stress recovers every nonquarantined loan.
Verification: Exhaustion, double release, foreign-pointer and conservation stress tests.
Configuration: Fixed block sizes/counts and maximum chain length.
Static budget: Exact pool bytes; no fallback allocator or unbounded chains.
Dependencies: NXR-002, NXR-054, NXR-058
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-061
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded socket-like endpoints
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional socket-like endpoints shall borrow generation-tagged boot slots, route calls through the owner worker and return timeout, closed and exhausted outcomes.
Acceptance: Exhaustion immediate; stale handles fail; closing rejects new requests and frees only after quiescence; timed-out callers regain buffers only after ownership resolution.
Verification: Exhaustion, stale ID, close/request races and timeout ownership tests.
Configuration: Optional endpoint subset; fixed endpoints/requests.
Static budget: Fixed endpoint records and staging; bounded loans allowed.
Dependencies: NXR-028, NXR-029, NXR-057, NXR-060
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-062
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Optional IPv4 baseline
STATEMENT: >>>
An IPv4 profile shall support static address, netmask, gateway and bounded ARP while rejecting malformed lengths/checksums before delivery.
Acceptance: Reject invalid address/mask combinations; malformed IPv4/ARP preserves unrelated state; ARP full evicts oldest-expired then oldest entry; fragmentation initially rejected/counted.
Verification: Static routing, ARP capacity/expiry and malformed packet tests.
Configuration: Optional IPv4; fixed ARP entries; fragmentation/reassembly disabled initially.
Static budget: Fixed ARP/routes; no fragment buffers; board total-memory gate.
Dependencies: NXR-058, NXR-059, NXR-060
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-063
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded DHCP client
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional DHCP shall use fixed per-interface lease state, capped retries/backoff and remove expired addresses before further application traffic.
Acceptance: Retry/backoff maxima respected; acquisition deadline reports no-address; expiry removes address; link loss pauses acquisition; malformed options do not overrun buffers.
Verification: Lease acquire/renew/expire, absent server, flaps and malformed options tests.
Configuration: Optional DHCPv4; fixed transactions, retry ceiling and acquisition deadline. Enables internal UDP without requiring public endpoints.
Static budget: One fixed client state and bounded message buffer/interface. Dedicated internal UDP PCB/slot reservation included.
Dependencies: NXR-056, NXR-059, NXR-062, NXR-066
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-064
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded DNS client
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional DNS shall use bounded names, fixed query/cache slots, response deadlines and bounded compression decoding.
Acceptance: Overlong names fail before send; full table returns busy; reply ID/source/question match; loops/depth excess fail; timeout releases once; cache evicts oldest-expired then oldest.
Verification: Query/cache exhaustion, timeout, mismatches and compression-loop corpus.
Configuration: Optional A records initially; fixed names/queries/cache and decode-step limit. Enables internal UDP without requiring public endpoints.
Static budget: Fixed query/cache/message bytes; no recursive allocation. Dedicated internal UDP PCB/slot reservation included.
