[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-065
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded TCP service
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional TCP shall enforce fixed connection, send/receive and retransmission budgets, expose partial progress and terminate retry exhaustion without leaking loans.
Acceptance: Connection/byte caps report pressure; loss retransmits within ceiling; timeout/reset/close releases or quarantines every loan; EOF/half-close differ from would-block.
Verification: Loss/reorder, capacity, partial I/O, retry exhaustion and close conservation tests.
Configuration: Optional TCP; fixed windows/segments/retries and close deadline.
Static budget: Fixed control blocks and windows; profiles may need larger board RAM.
Dependencies: NXR-059, NXR-060, NXR-061, NXR-062
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-066
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded UDP datagrams
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional UDP shall preserve datagram boundaries in fixed endpoint/RX slots, drop newest on full queues and report truncation explicitly.
Acceptance: One receive consumes one datagram; short destination reports copied/original lengths and discards remainder; full counts drop; malformed checksum/length rejects; send pressure preserves caller ownership. Internal UDP service is independently selectable from public endpoint API NXR-061; DHCP/DNS reservations are accounted separately and cannot be consumed by public endpoints.
Verification: Boundary/truncation, queue full, checksum and send-pressure tests.
Configuration: Optional UDP; fixed endpoints, queued datagrams and payload maximum.
Static budget: Fixed slots backed by packet loans; no growth.
Dependencies: NXR-057, NXR-059, NXR-060, NXR-062
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-067
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Coherent network health metrics
STATEMENT: >>>
Network metrics shall be captured by the owner into bounded snapshots with saturating accepted, discarded, busy, error, pool and link-generation counters.
Acceptance: No concurrent live 64-bit reads on RV32; counters never wrap; protocol rejection and hardware drops distinct; truncation reports required/written rows.
Verification: Traffic/snapshot, saturation, owner requests and truncation tests.
Configuration: Optional fixed snapshot capacity.
Static budget: Fixed counters and queued/caller snapshot storage; no formatting under critical paths.
Dependencies: NXR-050, NXR-057, NXR-060
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-068
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Coherent thread snapshots
STATEMENT: >>>
Thread snapshots shall copy coherent bounded identity, name, state, base/effective priority, current/idle rows with capacity reporting.
Acceptance: Null/zero returns required count; truncation never overruns; idle last after start; finished rows stable; donated priorities read atomically.
Verification: Target snapshot boundaries, priority changes, finished/idle and guarded-output tests.
Configuration: Snapshots available with metrics disabled; bounded rows.
Static budget: Caller rows; masked copy bounded by min(capacity, registered threads+idle).
Dependencies: NXR-006, NXR-017
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-069
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: CPU residency timer
STATEMENT: >>>
Enabled CPU metrics shall charge monotonic timer deltas exactly once and expose timer-cycle residency, dispatch counts and unassigned startup time.
Acceptance: At a common snapshot timestamp, thread residency plus explicit unassigned startup equals elapsed timer cycles. Accounting boundaries are the timestamp passed to account(); trap work before that boundary is charged outgoing and selection/restore after it incoming. Snapshot accounting advances the same boundary without double-counting. Units are timer cycles; CPU-cycle labeling requires verified timer-to-CPU ratio. Counters are monotonic within the 64-bit session horizon; disabled values zero; utilization rejects zero divisor/overflow.
Verification: Target conservation, repeated snapshots, idle/busy and disabled-profile tests.
Configuration: RTOS_METRICS; fixed-frequency hardware timer never reset or wrapped in session.
Static budget: Two 64-bit counters/thread and fixed globals; no floating point.
Dependencies: NXR-011, NXR-068
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-070
STATUS: PartialSourceUnverified
TITLE: Stack guard detection
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional guards shall initialize/check a sentinel at dispatch and diagnostic inspection, recording a bounded fault before halting on corruption.
Acceptance: Injected corruption detected at next check; disabled mode explicitly reports checking disabled; skipped sentinels/prior corruption limitations documented.
Verification: Target outgoing/incoming corruption and disabled-profile tests.
Configuration: RTOS_STACK_GUARD; no MPU/MMU claim.
Static budget: One word per stack plus fixed fault record.
Dependencies: NXR-003, NXR-007, NXR-073
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-071
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Incremental stack high-water sampling
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional watermarks shall fill unused boot stack regions and scan a configured byte budget per call without reading live saved-frame storage.
Acceptance: Known fill destruction yields conservative usage estimates; scans obey budget; initial fill excludes saved frame; concurrent execution cannot cause invalid reads; values labeled estimates. Scan only suspended noncurrent threads while holding a bounded scheduler lock; current-thread sampling is unavailable unless a target-safe self-capture mechanism is verified. No concurrent C++ stack accesses are permitted.
Verification: Fill/frame boundaries, budgets and deep-call/preemption sampling tests.
Configuration: Optional watermark; fixed fill and scan budget.
Static budget: No extra stack buffer; fixed cursor/lowest-observed index per thread.
Dependencies: NXR-003, NXR-007, NXR-068
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-072
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Fixed execution trace ring
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional tracing shall append fixed timestamped events to a boot ring with bounded writes, overwrite-oldest and lost-event counts.
Acceptance: Full overwrites oldest once and saturates loss count; committed records never torn; disabled mode removes storage/writes; extraction bounded without locked console I/O.
Verification: Wrap, preemption/extraction, saturation and disabled-build tests.
Configuration: Optional fixed event width, capacity and mask.
Static budget: Exact ring bytes and fixed indices/counters.
Dependencies: NXR-011, NXR-025
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-073
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded retained fault record
STATEMENT: >>>
Fault handling shall capture one fixed versioned reason, thread, CSR, timestamp and available frame record, freeze mutation and enter bounded halt/reset policy.
Acceptance: Unexpected/guard traps retain cause/PC; nested fault preserves first complete record; unavailable fields invalid; checksum detects partial retention; boot reports before clearing.
Verification: Trap, guard, nested-fault and partial-retention injection tests.
Configuration: Optional board retention region; halt/watchdog-reset policy.
Static budget: One fixed record; no allocation, blocking locks or unbounded output.
Dependencies: NXR-007, NXR-011
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-074
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Bounded service recovery
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional recovery shall use boot supervisor workers, quiesce ownership first and attempt a finite retry count before leaving service unavailable.
Acceptance: Failed quiescence quarantines; retries terminate; unrelated services progress; successful restart increments generation and rejects stale requests; no implicit thread/kernel restart.
Verification: Init/abort failure, retry ceiling, stale request and unrelated-service tests.
Configuration: Optional per-service retries, backoff and deadline.
Static budget: Boot workers and fixed recovery records; quarantine remains until reset-safe.
Dependencies: NXR-001, NXR-012, NXR-020, NXR-047, NXR-048, NXR-073
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NXR-075
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Optional tickless idle
STATEMENT: >>>
Optional tickless idle shall arm the earliest pending deadline only when no app is ready and reconcile ticks on wake without resetting hardware time.
Acceptance: No wake later than earliest deadline within granularity; early IRQ reconciles ticks; wrap/horizon/no-deadline cases bounded; RISCue WFI-NOP is not claimed to save energy. Earliest deadline includes enabled network protocol deadlines NXR-059; disabling networking removes that dependency at configuration time.
Verification: Early-wake, nearest-deadline, wrap, catch-up and metrics conservation tests.
Configuration: Optional tickless; maximum suppression <= INT32_MAX ticks.
Static budget: Fixed next-deadline metadata; bounded thread/timer scans.
